  <description>TE / Potter &amp; Brumfield T92 two-pole 30 A relay, 2 form A, 12 VDC coil, panel mount via flanged cover with .250 in (6.35 x 0.81 mm) quick-connect tabs. HYBRID PART: all six terminals are real in schematic and breadboard, so the coil driver and the mains nets connect normally and the sheet documents the real circuit - but every one is hybrid in pcbView, so there is no pad, no ratsnest and nothing to route on the board. The PCB gets the outline plus two mounting holes only, and those are non-plated: no copper, no net. Wire the contacts to the load with .250 in QC receptacles and bring the coil back to a 2-pin SELV terminal block. The flange plane is flush with the top of the case, so the relay stands on its flange and the body plus tabs rise 37.97 mm clear of the board - no board cutout and no standoffs are needed. Envelope 68.58 x 34.54 mm over the flanges, case 52.07 mm wide, mounting centres 59.56 +/- 0.13 mm, holes 4.5 mm for a #8 or M4 screw. Silkscreen tab marks are informational and mirrored to a top view; the real tabs sit 26.4 to 38.0 mm above the board. Footprint from TE datasheet 1308242 rev 1217, mounting and termination code 2.</description>
